I have been lurking in here for some time, and decided to post a YAAP for
this ascension.

jt the chaotic male elven wizard started with a book of remove curse, a
wand of fire, rings of slow digestion and conflict, and unremarkable
stuff. First move was taking off the [CoMR. Unfortunately, my pet died
on dungeon level 2 to a trap.

A following jackal lead to a problem as I tried to melee it but missed 8
times in succession, but the wand of fire saved me. I should have
forcebolted it of course.

Dungeon level 3 had a locked shop and a coaligned altar.

A giant bat on the next level brought me down to 12(25) hp, I had to use
the wand of fire again (not enough hp left for two more bites). One
melee hit, one melee miss and a force bolt were needed. The level also
had the mines entrance and a weapon shop.

Dungeon level 6 was the Oracle and had a little dog and a housecat. I
pacified the dog with a lichen corpse and tamed the cat.

A few killer bee swarms were scary -- without magic cancellation the
chance of deadly poison is pretty high. So I Elberethed and did not know
what to do for a moment. My pet was too far away. First I tried conflict
but it did not work well as a bee almost always (always?) misses a bee. I
decided to try to forcebolt two or more bees at a time (it has only 45%
chance of hitting a bee). I was left with enough corpses to fairly
certainly gain poison resistance but did not want to lose the strength :(

The first Sokoban level had a carrot in a pit. I fell into the pit to
pick it up, which turned out to be very useful to avoid spending
hundreds of turns blind without telepathy because of a yellow light.

I made an almost-fatal mistake with some Uruk-hai in standing like @fo,
almost dying from deadly poison. It was near the door. Unfortunately,
this meant I had to Elbereth and kill all the stuff myself. These orcs
will come back later :)

Next level had Uruk-hai again so I carefully avoided their line of fire
as much as possible. Some Elberething and the cat cleared them out and I
carried their arrows to prevent them from being used against me.

A red naga hatchling on the fourth Sokoban level finally provided poison
resistance. It was the "oR level. An important amulet for a naked
character, as it is the only practical way to get reflection (except for
a Ranger), and ray attacks do not miss as often because your AC is poor.
(turn 5548)

As I had no bag yet, I was getting in trouble with both Burdened and
inventory slots. So I just dropped food and spellbooks and useless crap.

Going back to the altar yielded Magicbane. A good Elbereth writer, and
it was my MR source. (I also had found a wand of create monster in
Sokoban.) (turn 7995)

A water prayer yielded speed (that is rare for me).

Minetown had a bag of holding and a magic whistle. The temple was
coaligned. My lamp was magic, but I did not know what to wish for. Some
sacrificing and a prayer gave me stealth and Sting. I robbed the stores
with the cat and bought 4 points of protection. After that I tried to
remove the watch captain by conflict with the priest but that killed the
priest instead.  I sacrificed the priest's corpse and I was rewarded
with a luck bonus.  (turn 12700)

The priest had books of sleep and healing, and the bookstore had
jumping. Both had some other spells as well.

A cockatrice was very scary, it could stone me while alive, and I
could not do anything with the corpse if killed. I lured it into a small
room, killed it there and locked the door.

The Mines below Minetown had many polytraps and I turned my cat into a
baby orange dragon.

Mines End was the Catacombs, with undead and some spellbooks. The dragon
was a big help here.

On the way back I turned a large dog into a winged gargoyle. These have
good AC and hit hard, clearing thronerooms while getting hardly hurt
themselves. (turn 16009)

The orange dragon stepped on a polytrap and turned into a horned devil,
and some time later the winged gargoyle turned into a wolf. I turned
them into slightly better monsters later.

A throne on DL 12 gave a wish and after some thought I chose 2 blessed
scrolls of genocide (stupid, I could have written those myself, plenty
of markers). One of those was immediately used to wipe out c.

Level 13 had the quest portal, but I was only XL 11. Charm monster
spell! (turn 20389)

On DL 19 I was suddenly next to a minotaur so I dug down (could have
charmed it too).

An Aleax on DL 20 was tamed.

Dungeon level 21 had a neutral temple, I lowered my AC to 1.

Dungeon level 26 was the Titan version of the Medusa level. Many of the
summoned nasties were tamed. I also tried to tame the titan but he
did not want to stay next to my Elberethed upstairs long enough, and was
killed by my pets. The eels were also killed by my pets. I levitated
over the water with a ring and killed Medusa with reflection.

So, I was there with XL 11, 78 HP, AC 1 and some good pets, like a
disenchanter, an Olog-hai, a purple worm and an Aleax. I decided to do
the castle while the pets were still alive. (turn 26328)

A few minotaurs in the mazes were slept and charmed, which made them
peaceful (not tame, for some reason).

Fortunately, the castle had no purple L. I used a wooden flute to open
and close the drawbridge many times, killing all sorts of monsters. I
did not have interest in the loot of the soldiers anyway. A disenchanter
and a guardian naga were tamed. This also tamed a giant eel.  I got the
wand of wishing, but still did not know what to wish for. (turn 27845)

I wrote a spellbook of detect monsters in the Valley of the Dead.

DL 31 had Asmodeus, who was paid off, for 18 zorkmids.

I did a few more levels with pets, magic missile and magic mapping.

On DL 34 I decided to go back up (turn 32480).

On DL 22 I reverse-genocided some wraiths. It did not seem likely to get
40k exp between two vampire bites. I locked myself in a room with my
non-eating pets. After that I was XL 16. I tried some graveyards for a
wraith corpse but they were all eaten by my pets, so I quaffed a potion
of gain level on DL 18. (turn 35440)

I moved my Minetown stash to Sokoban and collected the stuff I did not
have inventory slots for earlier, then refreshed some spells. I
enchanted Trollsbane to +5 but my Aleax did not want it for some reason
(even though I removed her long sword with a bullwhip), so my Elvenking
got it.

One of the quest levels had a spellbook of identify. I gave the Dark One
the Finger before he could pick up the Eye of the Aethiopica. That was
also the first time I cast that spell. (turn 39857)

Somewhere, the Aleax had stepped on a level teleporter to the quest home
level; it had to be retamed.

I went to the altar on 21 and let my pets kill the priest. The altar was
converted with a Woodland-elf corpse. (turn 41466)

I used up many wands and scrolls of create monster, and mainly got spellbooks
and golden glows. I went back to my Sokoban stash to get more wands and
scrolls, and eventually I wrote a spellbook of create monster. At turn
43414 I split a black pudding for the first time. I decided to go
pudding farming because it is more efficient. It still took more than
thousand turns after that to get the first point of protection from
prayer. Eventually, I had

Jt the Enchanter          St:18 Dx:18 Co:16 In:20 Wi:19 Ch:15 Chaotic
Dlvl:21 $:0  HP:227(227) Pw:183(183) AC:-8 Xp:17/850988 T:46856

and knew all spells.

With that, I mapped the rest of Gehennom.

A titan, tamed in Vlad's Tower, stepped on a polytrap very quickly and
turned into a gnome zombie. With careful use of conflict, I persuaded a
pet jabberwock to destroy it, as it remained rather long for my liking.

The Elvenking stepped on a level teleporter on the vibrating square
level; it took a long time to find that trap. The vibrating square was
marked with gold in the form of a plus sign and the Candelabrum. (turn
52420)

Alchemizing increased my hit points to 468. I wished up an Archon, which
came out tame just fine, and enchanted his Demonbane to +7. (It turns
out that it's better than Trollsbane against large opponents, besides,
demons are scarier than trolls.) I identified some of the Uruk-hai armor
(with the identify spell) and found a +4 orcish helm. The Archon also
got a unicorn horn and was fully leveled up by letting it kill puddings
on level 21.

I then went for the Wizard. A black dragon on the lower level of the
Wizard's Tower relieved me of some wimpier pets (OK, a purple worm too,
but anyway). The Wizard was killed for the first time on turn 54739.

The Sanctum was fairly uneventful and the Amulet was picked up on turn
54927. On the way up I had reduced my pet army to the Archon and one
purple worm. The pets were occasionally in the way, which made killing
the six Rodneys more challenging. The Force was not that bad, but I was
chaotic after all.

I took the stairs on level 1. Here I made a mistake not giving my Archon my
spare potions of gain level, that turned out to be rather hard on Astral. (turn
56304)

The planes of Earth and Fire were uneventful. On the plane of Air I used
up many wand of death charges for the elementals (I did not use conflict
because of the worm but it died anyway.)

Water was easy, I kept out a blessed scroll of genocide to wipe out ';' if
necessary but it was not necessary. I levitated over the water, as I
always do.

Astral required me to check all three altars before finding the chaotic
one. (I could not use a helm of opposite alignment.) Monsters were
teleported away or killed with pets, magic missiles or death rays.
Thanks to some healing spells the guardian Angel survived as well. Due
to some magical enhancement the Archon killed the high priests of the
wrong alignments.

After 56841 turns I offered the Amulet of Yendor. So while I think I
pudding-farmed quite a lot, it's still much less than what some other
people here seem to do routinely.

This ascension was not particularly hard, although I almost died at some
points. It is my first or one of my first serious attempts at naked
conduct.  Overall difficulty of the conduct seems similar to atheist or
illiterate.

